# Crypto / Web3 Rewards Cards — Gap-Fill Research

Research date: **2026-09-15**. Sources are live 2026 web reads (linked per row). `NEEDS RESEARCH` = no reliable figure found after a real attempt; **never a guess**.

**Key structural traps for MS / gold-buying:**
- **Costco warehouse = MCC 5300 "warehouse club," NOT MCC 5411 "grocery"** — so grocery-category bonuses generally exclude in-warehouse Costco. Separately, **US Costco warehouses take Visa only** — every Mastercard product below is unusable *in-warehouse* regardless of rewards.
- Nearly all crypto cards pay a **flat rate everywhere** (no grocery/warehouse category), so "Costco counts?" usually reduces to "is it Visa?"
- Most are **debit/prepaid**, so there is no credit-card bill to pay by debit (the Taekus-stack lever) — noted as `N/A - debit/prepaid`.
- **Reward-currency risk:** tokens like CRO, WXT, PLU, NEXO, XRP float in $ value; the headline % is denominated in that token, not dollars.

