## Notes / open items

- **Crypto.com 2026 "Level Up" overhaul:** in early 2026 Crypto.com began replacing the classic metallic tier *names* with a "Level Up" subscription model — non-stakers/non-subscribers now earn **0%**, and Plus/Pro subscriptions ($4.99/mo and $29.99/mo) are offered as an alternative to CRO staking. The 5 metallic tiers above use the canonical CRO-stake thresholds (5k / 50k / 500k / 5M CRO for 180 days) and their standard 1/2/3/5% rates; **current 2026 monthly cashback caps and whether each metallic rate survived the overhaul = NEEDS RESEARCH.** Sources: https://www.spendnode.io/blog/crypto-com-2026-card-overhaul-new-tiers/ , https://crypto.com/us/cards
- **US-available in 2026:** Coinbase, Crypto.com (prepaid tiers), Gemini, Venmo, Upgrade Bitcoin, Fold (debit + credit), Cash App, Robinhood Gold, Kraken/Krak, CoinZoom, Uphold (Elite/Essential), MetaMask (select states). **Not US:** Nexo, Wirex, Plutus, Bybit, Bitget, Club Swan, Ledger CL (verify). **Defunct/none:** BlockFi (bankrupt), Binance.US (no card), BitPay (new signups likely halted), Choice/Unchained (not a card).
- **Costco reality check:** among the *US Visa* crypto cards that could actually earn at a Costco warehouse — Coinbase, Venmo, Upgrade, Fold (both), Robinhood, Kraken, CoinZoom, Uphold — none carry a grocery/warehouse category bonus (all flat), so the "MCC 5300 trap" doesn't bite; they simply pay their flat rate. Gemini (2% grocery) and all Mastercard products are blocked in-warehouse by network.
- **Debit-pay lever (Taekus-stack):** only relevant for the *credit* cards — Gemini, Venmo, Upgrade Bitcoin, Fold Credit, Robinhood Gold. **Venmo = confirmed Yes** (debit/balance/bank). Robinhood = **No** (ACH only). Gemini, Upgrade, Fold Credit bill-pay-by-debit = **NEEDS RESEARCH** (Fold Credit gives +0.5% BTC for paying the bill *in bitcoin*, a different lever).
- **Token-denominated headline %:** Crypto.com (CRO), Wirex (WXT), Plutus (PLU), Nexo (NEXO), Uphold (XRP) pay in a volatile token — nominal % ≠ guaranteed $ back. BTC-back cards (Fold, Upgrade, Coinbase-choice, Kraken-choice) at least pay in bitcoin at market.
- **Not guessed:** every `NEEDS RESEARCH` reflects a real search that returned conflicting or absent data (e.g. Club Swan fee tiers, several FX fees, Ledger/MetaMask rates, current Crypto.com caps).
